-- title:
--   Finite part of the m-torsion of the Néron model
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$, both nonzero, with $p$ prime and $p \nmid N_0$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ (meaning $p$ is a non-unit of $A$), let $\Lambda$ be level data for $N_0,p,A$ satisfying the Jacobian conditions `IsJacobian`, let $O$ be a Néron object $\mathrm{JZeroNeronObjectAtP}$ for these data and let $F$ be a Néron extension of $O$, so $F$ carries a scheme $F.\mathrm{Nfull}$ with structure morphism $F.\mathrm{gN}$ over the valuation ring $\mathrm{shRing}\,A = A \cap \mathrm{invField}\,A$ of the fixed field of the inertia subgroup, a relative group law $F.\mathrm{LN}$, and the Néron model properties recorded in that structure; assume in addition that $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is an algebra over $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$ compatibly with $\mathrm{invField}\,A$ in a scalar tower. Let $m>0$. The assertion is the existence of a commutative ring $H_f$ with a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$ that is module-finite, flat and cocommutative, together with a morphism $\iota : \operatorname{Spec} H_f \to F.\mathrm{Nfull}$ and a bijection $e_f$ from the convolution monoid $\mathrm{WithConv}$ of $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$-algebra homomorphisms $H_f \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ onto the additive subgroup $F.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ of $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the level $N_0p$ modular function field generated by the $x$ that are $m$-torsion and satisfy $F.\mathrm{ExtN}\,x$, such that: the rank of $H_f$ over $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$ equals $\#\,F.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$; $\iota$ followed by $F.\mathrm{gN}$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map of $H_f$; for every commutative $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$-algebra $C$, all algebra maps $\varphi,\psi : H_f \to C$ and all sections $x,y$ of $F.\mathrm{gN}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $x = \operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $\iota$ and $y = \operatorname{Spec}\psi$ followed by $\iota$, the product $F.\mathrm{LN}.\mathrm{mul}\,x\,y$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the convolution product $\varphi * \psi$ followed by $\iota$; $e_f$ turns convolution into addition in $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0p)$; $e_f$ is equivariant for $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathrm{invField}\,A)$, in the sense that $e_f(\sigma\circ f) = \sigma\cdot e_f(f)$ under the $\mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$-action; and for every $f : H_f \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\operatorname{Spec} f$ followed by $\iota$ is the section $F.\mathrm{ptsN}(e_f(f))$, obtained by lifting $O.\mathrm{pts}$ of that point along the open immersion of $F$.
--
--   This realises the finite part of the quasi-finite flat kernel of multiplication by $m$ on the Néron model over the henselian base $\mathrm{shRing}\,A$ as the spectrum of a finite flat commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra, whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points match, compatibly with the group laws and with the Galois action, the subgroup of $m$-torsion divisor classes extending over the place. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the associated bialgebra homomorphisms over the local base, and hence the local study of the $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$ at $p$.
